<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Zhongzong of Tang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/656">656</a>–710</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Li Xian, Li Zhe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Zhongzong of Tang (656–710) was a son of Emperor Gaozong and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian">Wu Zetian</a>. He succeeded his father at the end of 683 but was deposed by his mother early in 684 and sent into exile. Restored by the coup of 705 that ended Wu Zetian's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>, he was dominated by his wife Empress Wei and died suddenly in 710, reputedly poisoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-zhongzong-of-tang.jpg" alt="Emperor Zhongzong of Tang" width="200" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Because the artists have died over 100 years, so unknown. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tang_Zhongzong.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
